Subject: [PATCH] Stats: avoid citext regex splitting for peer domains

User nicknames are citext, whose split_part overload uses a case-insensitive
regular expression. Peer domains only need splitting on a literal '@'.
Cast to text and use string_to_array instead, preserving NULL for a missing
second component and avoiding the regex work on every remote user.

---
 lib/pleroma/stats.ex | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/pleroma/stats.ex b/lib/pleroma/stats.ex
--- a/lib/pleroma/stats.ex
+++ b/lib/pleroma/stats.ex
@@ -67,7 +67,7 @@ defmodule Pleroma.Stats do
     peers =
       from(
         u in User,
-        select: fragment("distinct split_part(?, '@', 2)", u.nickname),
+        select: fragment("distinct (pg_catalog.string_to_array(?::text, '@'))[2]", u.nickname),
         where: u.local != ^true
       )
       |> Repo.all()
